{"qid":"Q790","names":["Republic of Haiti"],"title":"Republic of Haiti","endonym":{"native":"Ayiti","lang":"ht"},"capsule":"Haiti occupies the western third of Hispaniola and was the first Black republic in the world, declaring independence on 1 January 1804 after a slave revolution that expelled French colonial forces under Jean-Jacques Dessalines. In the twentieth century the Duvalier family dictatorship (François, 1957–71; Jean-Claude, 1971–86) entrenched predatory rule backed by the Tonton Macoutes paramilitary. A series of contested elections, military coups, and international interventions—including the 1994 U.S. restoration of President Jean-Bertrand Aristide—marked the post-Duvalier period; a catastrophic earthquake on 12 January 2010 killed an estimated 160,000–316,000 people and set back decades of development.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Haiti's national borders are well-defined and stable since independence; territorial extent is certain.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Haiti","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haiti"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Haitian Revolution","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haitian_Revolution"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 2010 Haiti earthquake","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2010_Haiti_earthquake"},{"label":"Wikipedia: François Duvalier","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fran%C3%A7ois_Duvalier"}],"britannica":"place/Haiti","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Haiti","rulers":[{"qid":"Q886213","name":"Stenio Vincent","start":1930,"end":1941,"image":"Stenio Vincent portrait.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Stenio%20Vincen